sponge cake and meringue into two layers. Put the nut meringue on top of the bottom layer of sponge and sprinkle on some of the reserved walnuts. Add another layer of meringue and then the upper layer of chocolate sponge cake and cover the top with chocolate glaze. Decorate with walnuts. Put the finished cake in the fridge for 1-2 hrs before serving.	4	\N	Polish	["перекус"]	t	https://www.bbcgoodfood.com/recipes/polish-chocolate-cake	mealdb:53295	[{"id": "6ce07f42-79ab-4850-9b60-2e28639d6e07", "name": "Пшеничная мука", "unit": "г", "grams": 65, "amount": 65, "ingredientId": "89fd83a9-9424-4975-a81b-218d640c70a2", "originalString": "65 г"}, {"id": "ea117af4-116d-4667-88d3-5af3e876ad01", "name": "Коко-сахар", "unit": "г", "grams": 50, "amount": 50, "ingredientId": "1e027bee-2628-4fd9-ae2e-6d9c175587f3", "originalString": "50 г"}, {"id": "eceb523c-2d44-4cf3-bcbc-9e5307a5402a", "name": "Яйцо", "unit": "г", "grams": 400, "amount": 400, "ingredientId": "cab42edd-5e3a-4893-839e-9f4ef50c6cf0", "originalString": "400 г"}, {"id": "137c472c-4f48-4fe8-8532-977b6f875deb", "name": "Сахарная пудра", "unit": "г", "grams": 100, "amount": 100, "ingredientId": "0ae3eca4-e36e-42f4-ae8e-a3f42bcb8501", "originalString": "100 г"}, {"id": "feaa344a-2780-48c7-8392-194d9a60a365", "name": "Яичный белок", "unit": "г", "grams": 250, "amount": 250, "ingredientId": "b0a5521a-55a8-42b0-84f7-bbf2f5e48c6f", "originalString": "250 г"}, {"id": "126805de-9c8d-45f4-b4e4-8aeffaebec17", "name": "Грецкие орехи", "unit": "г", "grams": 50, "amount": 50, "ingredientId": "943fa0a9-f332-42c8-927b-e37fb168b420", "originalString": "50 г"}, {"id": "02e13510-db13-4b66-ae92-fe5aa6a651bc", "name": "Густые сливки", "unit": "мл", "grams": 50, "amount": 50, "ingredientId": "bbff168c-afd7-44e8-98cf-111d7e0af483", "originalString": "50 мл"}, {"id": "afb0afe3-2396-4345-a393-09ed4a281bfe", "name": "Шоколадные чипсы", "unit": "г", "grams": 50, "amount": 50, "ingredientId": "dfc11d30-0b79-4326-b5f7-1f369ed1f3fd", "originalString": "50 г"}, {"id": "72ad8347-33ea-4d4c-a6ac-91d26c29dcc9", "name": "Картофельный крахмал", "unit": "г", "grams": 15, "amount": 15, "ingredientId": "d2ffa218-8a62-4257-b818-35c8650a8b94", "originalString": "15 г"}]	["vegetarian"]	t	\N
493d4551-097c-4fa2-886e-6cc3de4728d5	Курица по-ямайски с рисом и горохом	lunch	600	35.8	26.9	51.9	{лактоза,соя}	[{"name": "Куриные бёдра", "grams": 600}, {"name": "Лайм", "grams": 100}, {"name": "Зелёный лук", "grams": 75}, {"name": "Имбирь", "grams": 60}, {"name": "Чеснок", "grams": 250}, {"name": "Лук", "grams": 75}, {"name": "Красный чили", "grams": 180}, {"name": "Тимьян", "grams": 3}, {"name": "Соевый соус", "grams": 120}, {"name": "Растительное масло", "grams": 120}, {"name": "Коричневый сахар", "grams": 180}, {"name": "Allspice", "grams": 120}, {"name": "Рис басмати", "grams": 60}, {"name": "Кокосовое молоко", "grams": 60}, {"name": "Фасоль красная", "grams": 5}]	https://www.themealdb.com/images/media/meals/tytyxu1515363282.jpg	2026-05-03 20:14:19.824+00	2026-10-06 13:02:27.083+00	["куриные", "курин", "бедра", "лайм", "зеленый", "зелен", "лук", "имбирь", "имбир", "чеснок", "чесно", "красный", "красн", "чили", "тимьян", "тимья", "соевый", "соевы", "соев", "соус", "растительное", "расти", "растительн", "масло", "коричневый", "корич", "коричнев", "сахар", "allspice", "allsp", "рис", "басмати", "басма", "кокосовое", "кокос", "кокосов", "молоко", "молок", "фасоль", "фасол", "красная"]	To make the jerk marinade, combine all the ingredients in a food processor along with 1 tsp salt, and blend to a pur├йe. If youтАЩre having trouble getting it to blend, just keep turning off the blender, stirring the mixture, and trying again. Eventually it will start to blend up тАУ donтАЩt be tempted to add water, as you want a thick paste.\r\n\r\nTaste the jerk mixture for seasoning тАУ it should taste pretty salty, but not unpleasantly, puckering salty. You can now throw in more chillies if itтАЩs not spicy enough for you. If it tastes too salty and sour, try adding in a bit more brown sugar until the mixture tastes well balanced.\r\n\r\nMake a few slashes in the chicken thighs and pour the marinade over the meat, rubbing it into all the crevices. Cover and leave to marinate overnight in the fridge.\r\n\r\nIf you want to barbecue your chicken, get the coals burning 1 hr or so before youтАЩre ready to cook. Authentic jerked meats are not exactly grilled as we think of grilling, but sort of smoke-grilled. To get a more authentic jerk experience, add some wood chips to your barbecue, and cook your chicken over slow, indirect heat for 30 mins. To cook in the oven, heat to 180C/160C fan/gas 4. Put the chicken pieces in a roasting tin with the lime halves and cook for 45 mins until tender and cooked through.\r\n\r\nWhile the chicken is cooking, prepare the rice & peas. Rinse the rice in plenty of cold water, then tip it into a large saucepan with all the remaining ingredients except the kidney beans. Season with salt, add 300ml cold water and set over a high heat. Once the rice begins to boil, turn it down to a medium heat, cover and cook for 10 mins.\r\n\r\nAdd the beans to the rice, then cover with a lid. Leave off the heat for 5 mins until all the liquid is absorbed. Squeeze the roasted lime over the chicken and serve with the rice & peas, and some hot sauce if you like it really spicy.	6	\N	Jamaican	["ужин"]	t	https://www.bbcgoodfood.com/recipes/2369635/jerk-chicken-with-rice-and-peas	mealdb:52937	[{"id": "ce642fcd-c46d-4a33-a62e-8fa18be36fd8", "name": "Куриные бёдра", "unit": "г", "grams": 600, "amount": 600, "ingredientId": "4408ccda-a27e-4db6-bc16-bef8099e89a5", "originalString": "600 г"}, {"id": "170a28ab-8fad-4dfa-89a5-4cb98751261c", "name": "Лайм", "unit": "г", "grams": 75, "amount": 75, "ingredientId": "d69a6d78-fb1a-455e-8c7a-0fb3887dfa17", "originalString": "75 г"}, {"id": "4a6708a1-85be-47d0-8985-9774dd9b0cdc", "name": "Зелёный лук", "unit": "г", "grams": 100, "amount": 100, "ingredientId": "e15bcbde-b1b4-4df4-a673-98865ea67f17", "originalString": "100 г"}, {"id": "ef284cf9-13c7-4144-935e-f9eeac2b71f5", "name": "Имбирь", "unit": "г", "grams": 50, "amount": 50, "ingredientId": "245533a8-d5cb-4feb-9254-2f888a3b4f85", "originalString":