1c9529ef-e4b4-441e-aaeb-29393bf39dc7	Овощной пирог пастушонка	dinner	413	15.1	13.1	53.8	{лактоза,глютен,соя}	[{"name": "Картофель", "grams": 150}, {"name": "Маленький картофель", "grams": 150}, {"name": "Соленое масло", "grams": 120}, {"name": "Грибы", "grams": 50}, {"name": "Коричневая чечевица", "grams": 180}, {"name": "Чеснок", "grams": 300}, {"name": "Кошерная соль", "grams": 5}, {"name": "Лук", "grams": 750}, {"name": "Томатное пюре", "grams": 120}, {"name": "Лавровый лист", "grams": 3}, {"name": "Оливковое масло", "grams": 60}, {"name": "Сухое белое вино", "grams": 480}, {"name": "Овощной бульон", "grams": 1920}, {"name": "Кукурузный крахмал", "grams": 60}, {"name": "Соевый соус", "grams": 60}, {"name": "Розмарин", "grams": 3}, {"name": "Петрушка", "grams": 60}, {"name": "Шалфей", "grams": 60}, {"name": "Шнитт-лук", "grams": 75}]	https://www.themealdb.com/images/media/meals/w8umt11583268117.jpg	2026-05-03 20:14:11.966+00	2026-10-06 13:10:30.382+00	["картофель", "карто", "маленький", "мален", "маленьк", "соленое", "солен", "масло", "грибы", "коричневая", "корич", "коричнев", "чечевица", "чечев", "чеснок", "чесно", "кошерная", "кошер", "кошерн", "соль", "лук", "томатное", "томат", "томатн", "пюре", "лавровый", "лавро", "лавров", "лист", "оливковое", "оливк", "оливков", "сухое", "сух", "белое", "бел", "вино", "овощной", "овощн", "бульон", "бульо", "кукурузный", "кукур", "кукурузн", "крахмал", "крахм", "соевый", "соевы", "соев", "соус", "розмарин", "розма", "петрушка", "петру", "шалфей", "шалфе", "шалф", "шнитт"]	Add Ingredients:\r\n\r\n12 cups chopped mixed vegetables\r\n1   cup chopped fresh mushrooms \r\n1   cup pearl onions\r\n\r\nTOPPING:\r\n\r\nPreheat oven to 450┬░. Bake potatoes on a foil-lined baking sheet until tender, about 45 minutes. Let cool slightly, then peel. Press potatoes through a ricer, food mill, or colander into a large bowl. Add butter; stir until well blended. Stir in milk. Season to taste with salt.\r\n\r\nFILLING:\r\n\r\nSoak dried porcini in 3 cups hot water; set aside. Combine lentils, 1 garlic clove, 1 tsp. salt, and 4 cups water in a medium saucepan. Bring to a boil; reduce heat and simmer, stirring occasionally, until lentils are tender but not mushy, 15тАУ20 minutes. Drain lentils and discard garlic.\r\n\r\nHeat 3 Tbsp. oil in a large heavy pot over medium heat. Add onions and cook, stirring occasionally, until soft, about 12 minutes. Add chopped garlic and cook for 1 minute. Stir in tomato paste. Cook, stirring constantly, until tomato paste is caramelized, 2тАУ3 minutes.\r\n\r\nAdd bay leaves and wine; stir, scraping up any browned bits. Stir in porcini, slowly pouring porcini soaking liquid into pan but leaving any sediment behind. Bring to a simmer and cook until liquid is reduced by half, about 10 minutes. Stir in broth and cook, stirring occasionally, until reduced by half, about 45 minutes.\r\n\r\nStrain mixture into a large saucepan and bring to a boil; discard solids in strainer. Stir cornstarch and 2 Tbsp. water in a small bowl to dissolve. Add cornstarch mixture; simmer until thickened, about 5 minutes. Whisk in miso. Season sauce with salt and pepper. Set aside.\r\n\r\nPreheat oven to 450┬░. Toss vegetables and pearl onions with remaining 2 Tbsp. oil, 5 garlic cloves, and rosemary sprigs in a large bowl; season with salt and pepper. Divide between 2 rimmed baking sheets. Roast, stirring once, until tender, 20тАУ25 minutes. Transfer garlic cloves to a small bowl; mash well with a fork and stir into sauce. Discard rosemary. DO AHEAD: Lentils, sauce, and vegetables can be made 1 day ahead. Cover separately; chill.\r\nArrange lentils in an even layer in a 3-qt. baking dish; set dish on a foil-lined rimmed baking sheet. Toss roasted vegetables with fresh mushrooms and chopped herbs; layer on top of lentils. Pour sauce over vegetables. Spoon potato mixture evenly over.\r\n\r\nBake until browned and bubbly, about 30 minutes. Let stand for 15 minutes before serving.	8	\N	Irish	["ужин"]	t	