": "Сахар", "unit": "г", "grams": 50, "amount": 50, "ingredientId": "f686d932-ccf2-4d50-9f23-2e0375fdd9d4", "originalString": "50 г"}, {"id": "c99ca07e-79d5-4bd4-acc5-3e0c22871eec", "name": "Мука", "unit": "г", "grams": 50, "amount": 50, "ingredientId": "6b9d37d6-50b6-41f6-bc22-2376d8109821", "originalString": "50 г"}, {"id": "0283830a-f936-4fd0-a1d7-eb2c4f12cbd3", "name": "Соль", "unit": "г", "grams": 50, "amount": 50, "ingredientId": "3789cffa-31e4-49d0-bca4-aded4002f42c", "originalString": "50 г"}, {"id": "9c4b0dc3-16a8-42ab-94c3-b25fc9a1baa1", "name": "Dulce de leche", "unit": "г", "grams": 50, "amount": 50, "ingredientId": "6aee8b0d-e361-49fb-b868-7bd294249194", "originalString": "50 г"}, {"id": "10d49631-50e4-494b-ac85-1feb9192fbea", "name": "Горький шоколад", "unit": "г", "grams": 50, "amount": 50, "ingredientId": "f718c6ca-2e52-49c6-8d7d-150737fdb6dc", "originalString": "50 г"}, {"id": "7a67d123-4f6a-4ff8-a13b-a1799684f312", "name": "Яйцо", "unit": "шт", "grams": 55, "amount": 1, "ingredientId": "cab42edd-5e3a-4893-839e-9f4ef50c6cf0", "originalString": "1 шт"}]	["vegetarian", "lactose-free"]	t	\N
f4b3f44d-b187-4e9c-a201-005a6bb85fe7	Гороховый суп	lunch	524	24.3	10.2	84	{глютен,лактоза}	[{"name": "Красная фасоль", "grams": 5}, {"name": "Морковь", "grams": 80}, {"name": "Зеленый лук", "grams": 75}, {"name": "Тимьян", "grams": 3}, {"name": "Лук", "grams": 75}, {"name": "Черный перец", "grams": 3}, {"name": "Красный перец", "grams": 3}, {"name": "Чеснок", "grams": 200}, {"name": "Душистый перец", "grams": 3}, {"name": "Говядина", "grams": 120}, {"name": "Вода", "grams": 120}, {"name": "Картофель", "grams": 150}, {"name": "Пшеничная мука", "grams": 240}, {"name": "Кокосовое молоко", "grams": 240}]	https://www.themealdb.com/images/media/meals/sqpqtp1515365614.jpg	2026-05-03 20:14:09.353+00	2026-10-06 13:02:27.462+00	["красная", "красн", "фасоль", "фасол", "морковь", "морко", "зеленый", "зелен", "лук", "тимьян", "тимья", "черный", "черны", "черн", "перец", "красный", "чеснок", "чесно", "душистый", "душис", "душист", "говядина", "говяд", "вода", "картофель", "карто", "пшеничная", "пшени", "пшеничн", "мука", "кокосовое", "кокос", "кокосов", "молоко", "молок"]	Wash and rinse the dried kidney beans.. then cover with water in a deep bowl. Remember as they soak they will expand to at least triple the size they were originally so add a lot of water to the bowl. Soak them overnight or for at least 2 hrs to make the cooking step go quicker. I tossed out the water they were soaked in after it did the job.\r\n\r\nHave your butcher cut the salted pigtail into 2 inch pieces as it will be very difficult to cut with an ordinary kitchen knife. Wash, then place a deep pot with water and bring to a boil. Cook for 20 minutes, then drain + rinse and repeat (boil again in water). The goal is to make the pieces of pig tails tender and to remove most of the salt it was cured in.\r\n\r\nTime to start the soup. Place everything in the pot (except the flour and potato), then cover with water and place on a high flame to bring to a boil. As it comes to a boil, skim off any scum/froth at the top and discard. Reduce the heat to a gentle boil and allow it to cook for 1 hr and 15 mins.. basically until the beans are tender and start falling apart.\r\n\r\nItтАЩs now time to add the potato (and Yams etc if youтАЩre adding it) as well as the coconut milk and continue cooking for 15 minutes.\r\n\r\nNow is a good time to start making the basic dough for the spinner dumplings. Mix the flour and water (add a pinch of salt if you want) until you have a soft/smooth dough. allow it to rest for 5 minutes, then pinch of a tablespoon at a time and roll between your hands to form a cigarette shape.\r\n\r\nAdd them to the pot, stir well and continue cooking for another 15 minutes on a rolling boil.\r\n\r\nYouтАЩll notice that I didnтАЩt add any salt to the pot as the remaining salt from the salted pigtails will be enough to properly season this dish. However you can taste and adjust accordingly. Lets recap the timing part of things so youтАЩre not confused. Cook the base of the soup for 1 hr and 15 minute or until tender, then add the potatoes and cook for 15 minutes, then add the dumplings and cook for a further 15 minutes. Keep in mind that this soup will thicken quite a bit as it cools.\r\n\r\nWhile this is not a traditional recipe to any one specific island, versions of this soup (sometimes called stewed peas) can be found throughout the Caribbean, Latin America and Africa. A hearty bowl of this soup will surely give you the sleepies (some may call it ethnic fatigue). You can certainly freeze the leftovers and heat it up another day.	3	\N	Jamaican	["ужин"]	t	http://caribbeanpot.com/caribbean-red-peas-soup/	mealdb:52941	[{"id": "20cde49a-0658-4cec-8324-2d54323d1d55", "name": "Красная фасоль", "unit": "г", "grams": 480, "amount": 480, "ingredientId": "1054a85d-75a8-4310-9753-5b4b9f98378f", "originalString": "480 г"}, {"id": "fa19e1ae-8e6d-49ac-ba3c-2bae5a04ae9e", "name": "Морковь", "unit": "г", "grams": 50, "amount": 50, "ingredientId": "3ab14c63-202a-4334-b30c-9674ce7